<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=spinning-jenny">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spinning jenny</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1764–<a href="/years/1765">1765</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The spinning jenny is a multi-spindle spinning frame invented in 1764–1765 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-hargreaves">James Hargreaves</a> at Stanhill, Oswaldtwistle, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lancashire">Lancashire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. One worker could work eight or more spools at once, a number that later grew to 120, which helped meet the weavers' demand for yarn after the flying shuttle. Hargreaves patented it in 1770; it produced coarse thread and was superseded by the spinning mule, but it helped start the factory system of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> manufacturing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spinning-jenny.jpg" alt="Spinning jenny" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Markus Schweiß · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spinning_jenny.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 1764</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Stanhill, Lancashire, England</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/encyclopedia/james-hargreaves">James Hargreaves</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Thomas Highs of Leigh has claimed to be the inventor, and a myth credits Thomas Earnshaw with a similar device that he destroyed.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/spinning-wheel">Spinning wheel<span>2nd century CE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=spinning-jenny">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
